the formatting engine
=====================

yupiter_printf and yupiter_fprintf are thin wrappers around
yupiter_vfprintf.  On failure the staged output is discarded; on
success it is flushed.  Direct writes to the kernel cannot be
discarded and are only used for unbuffered streams or payloads larger
than the staging buffer.  Everything else is in io/vfprintf.cxx.

The engine is C++23 with C linkage; internal helpers are in an
anonymous namespace.


Flow
----

One call: parse the format string, format each conversion, stage bytes,
flush on success.  Parser and formatter share one translation unit so
the full specification is known before any byte is emitted.  State per
call: stream, character count, sticky failure flag.  First failure
stops the call.


Dialect
-------

Conversions: %d %i %u %o %x %X %c %s %p %%.  Flags: - + space 0 #.
Width and precision via number or *.  Length modifiers: hh h l ll z t j.
Field width and precision are bounded; out-of-range values are clamped.

Not supported: floating point, positional arguments, %n, I/' flags.
Unrecognised conversions consume their argument and emit nothing.


Format checking
---------------

yupiter_printf and yupiter_fprintf carry a format attribute, so
mismatched arguments are caught at compile time.  Cases that need
undefined or rejected behaviour are called through a function pointer.